7. Risk Management Framework
Risk management is not a post-hoc constraint layer — it is co-designed with the signal generation architecture. Every order that reaches the broker must pass through a multi-stage risk gate that enforces both pre-trade and real-time controls.
7.1 Position Sizing — Volatility Targeting
The primary position sizing method is volatility targeting, which maintains constant portfolio-level volatility regardless of individual asset volatility:
TargetVol = 0.10 (10% annualized portfolio volatility target)
DailyTargetVol = TargetVol / √252
Position_i = (Allocation_i × DailyTargetVol) / HV(20, asset_i)
where HV(20) = 20-day realized volatility of asset_i
This automatically reduces size in high-volatility environments (protecting capital) and increases size in calm environments (maximizing capital efficiency).
7.2 Pre-Trade Risk Gate — Checks
8.	Position concentration: reject any new order that would cause single-asset weight > 10% of NAV.
9.	Sector concentration: reject if any GICS sector weight would exceed 25% of NAV.
10.	Gross leverage: reject if total long + short notional / NAV > 2.0×.
11.	Net leverage: reject if (long − short notional) / NAV > 1.5×.
12.	VaR limit: reject if order would cause 1-day 95% portfolio VaR > 2% NAV.
13.	Correlation check: reject if new position's rolling 60-day correlation with largest existing position > 0.85.
14.	Minimum liquidity: reject if order size > 5% of 20-day ADV.
7.3 Real-Time Drawdown Controls
Drawdown Level	Action
Daily P&L < −1.5% NAV	Alert risk officer; freeze new position openings for 30 minutes
Rolling 5-day P&L < −3% NAV	Reduce all positions by 50%; escalate to senior risk
MDD from equity peak > −10%	Halt all new trades; notify management; manual override required to resume
MDD from equity peak > −20%	Full position liquidation; system lockdown until root-cause review

7.4 Tail Risk Hedging
•	Systematic VIX futures overlay: buy VIX call spreads when implied volatility is below the 20th percentile of its 1-year distribution (cheap optionality).
•	Correlation breakdown monitor: if cross-asset correlation spiking above 0.7 (crisis indicator), increase cash buffer by 20%.
•	Black Swan reserve: 2% of NAV held in deep OTM put options on SPY at all times.
 
