12. Security, Compliance & Operational Procedures
12.1 Security Architecture
•	Network: All inter-service communication encrypted with TLS 1.3. Kubernetes Network Policies restrict pod-to-pod traffic to explicitly allowed paths only. No service exposes ports directly to the internet.
•	Authentication: OAuth 2.0 + PKCE for dashboard users; mutual TLS for service-to-service gRPC calls. API keys rotated every 30 days via Vault.
•	Authorization: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) with roles: admin, trader, analyst, read-only. Least-privilege principle applied to all service accounts and IAM roles.
•	Secrets: Zero secrets in code or environment variables in production. All credentials retrieved at runtime from HashiCorp Vault with dynamic short-lived tokens.
•	Audit Logging: Every order submission, risk gate decision, and configuration change is immutably logged with user identity, timestamp, and before/after state.
12.2 Regulatory Considerations
•	Pattern Day Trader (PDT) rule: system tracks rolling 5-day round-trip trades for accounts < $25K; alerts when approaching PDT threshold.
•	Wash sale tracking: trades in the same security within 30 days of a loss are flagged for tax reporting purposes.
•	Short-sale restrictions: system queries SEC locate requirements and checks borrow availability before submitting short orders.
•	Market manipulation prevention: order rate limiters ensure no strategy submits > 50 orders per minute per symbol.
•	Broker compliance: all order types and quantities validated against broker-specific constraints before submission.
12.3 Disaster Recovery
